    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get the \"middle ground\" argument, but the committee is looking for something more decisive. People often argue that you can't actually have both—that adding pathways to citizenship creates a \"pull factor\" that undermines enforcement, or that heavy enforcement just creates a humanitarian crisis that's impossible to manage. \n\nIf you had to pick the more \"realistic\" pillar to build a foundation on first, which one is more essential for actual stability? Is it the security side or the legal pathway side?",
